{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "bi8Au",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Admin / Brief / Happy path band",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "fill": "$surface-container",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 22,
      "padding": 36,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "a3lK0",
          "name": "Flow title",
          "fill": "$on-surface",
          "content": "Admin — the operator's dashboard",
          "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
          "fontSize": 24,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "tYURy",
          "name": "Kit pin",
          "fill": "$outline",
          "content": "kit-version-source 0.2.0 · band 1 of 1 · happy path · 6 of 6 screens drawn",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "XiA6X",
          "name": "Purpose",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "m1I82",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Purpose",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Z30eK",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Sign in is the front door — the screen an installed dashboard shows every time the 12-hour session ends, and the only one that must render when the rest of the admin cannot. Behind it, five pages sit under one sidebar, read left to right in nav order. Overview answers what is failing, how much headroom is left, what is running now, how slow it is, what it cost and what traffic looked like. Request Logs is where the operator lives — every Overview error row links into it, pre-filtered. API Keys is who may call and what they spent. Playground sends a real request through the real /v1 path with a real key. System is what is running and which providers are allowed to answer.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "ySQXf",
          "name": "Entry points",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "PcPRv",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Entry points",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "lt8bE",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "/admin/login — the sign-in page, src/admin/login.js, where every unauthenticated request lands; its next parameter returns the operator to the tab the session died on. /admin/dashboard/ — Overview is the default page; the five sidebar items are src/admin/public/js/app.js:209. Two real transitions exist and both are drawn as destinations: Overview → Logs via openErrorLogs(), which puts a filter in the nav store before setting location.hash, and API Keys → Logs via openKeyLogs().",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "s7ZA9",
          "name": "Screens in this band",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "CQ2Jw",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Screens in this band",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "vbl2W",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Six screens, all at dac0bc6: Sign in / Default, Overview / Default, Request Logs / Default, API Keys / Default, Playground / Answered, System / Default. Two carry an expanded sub-state rather than a screen of their own — Logs shows its third row expanded (where request_id, upstream status and the cache counters live) and API Keys shows its third key in edit (where the 'rotate replaces the secret' rule is stated). Playground is drawn answered rather than idle, because the idle state is one sentence ('Nothing sent yet.') and the answered state is the layout. Overview alone carries the 1440×900 fold marker (grid-fold-y): it is the only screen whose content runs past the declared frame, so it is the only one where the fold falls inside something.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "gskz5",
          "name": "Business rules",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "UrSK7",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Business rules",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "maNao",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "One window everywhere a figure is aggregated: every request the pruner has not deleted, bounded at 30 days. No period selector — removed 2026-09-20. Overview's two charts share one time axis from the oldest surviving request to just past now; quiet hours are zero, not skipped. Logs paginates server-side (25/50/100) and its two panels read that same window, which is why they no longer claim '60m' or 'today'. API Keys reports usage over its own 7d window, set server-side and printed in the column header. Playground authenticates like any other caller — same key, same rate limit, same log row — and deliberately does not use apiFetch, so a 401 there reads as a refused client key rather than an expired admin session. Pausing a provider on System takes it out of routing; it does not sign it out.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "otdq2",
          "name": "Copy source",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "MqB2L",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Copy source",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "F7BCS8",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "src/admin/views/pages/*.html verbatim, plus index.html for the shell and src/admin/login.js for Sign in. Numbers are illustrative; every label, verdict sentence, note and empty-state string is the code's. Timestamps render in SHELLM_TZ, default America/Mexico_City. The logo is mirrored from logo-dark.svg, which is SVG text rather than artwork: '>_ ' in mono, 'She' and 'M' in white, 'LL' in primary-container. Sign in ships its own self-contained <style> and sets everything in the mono stack — it shares no stylesheet with the dashboard, which is D20.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "P2Kx9l",
          "name": "States not drawn",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ia1G8",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "States not drawn",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "anChz",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Sign in has two states this band does not draw, both one panel appended to the same form: 401 'Invalid credentials' and 429 'Too many failed attempts. Try again in Ns.' — a paragraph with a 3px left border in error, on surface-container-lowest, below the button. They belong to the error band this flow does not have yet. Loading and unreachable are one-line string swaps that carry no layout these screens lack — 'Loading stats...', 'Could not read the logs — …', 'No logs found', 'No keys created yet'. System's providers section now has all three, drawn as a single line each, and a refused provider toggle says which provider did not change; the failure states themselves are not drawn for the same reason as the rest. The degraded banner ('Not updating' + the connection message + last read) sits in main above every page and is conditional. USAGE LIMIT HIT is a conditional banner above Capacity. Playground's running state — 'Waiting for the CLI…' with 'stop waiting' beside it — is the state D11 created and is NOT drawn here: this screen is Answered, and showing both would claim the answer arrived while the page is still waiting. Overview's CHART INTERIORS are not mirrored at all: Chart.js draws a scatter and a line, the .pen layout cannot position individual points, and an approximation would look plausible while misrepresenting what ships. Two of Sign in's four CRT layers are repeating patterns the canvas cannot tile and carry a note on the artboard instead. The Logs sparkline IS drawn — fifteen divs with computed heights is something the layout can express honestly.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "E1ghK",
          "name": "Open findings",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "dGbav",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Open findings",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "NgWjW",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "D16 · D18 · D20 remain. D20 is now visible on the canvas: Sign in is drawn from its own nine aliases, pinned to the canonical values by a test, and the kit is not asked to pretend otherwise. D30 (this screen was undrawn) closes with this pass — the code led for once, and the Log says so. D15, D17 and D19 closed 2026-09-20. D16 is still live on Playground: the catalog notes go silent on a failed read, in the one panel whose job is provenance. One kit gap surfaced here and is NOT fixed in the kit: the sweep gradient needs a fully transparent stop, and the kit has no token for one, so #03e3ff00 is the only hex in this flow.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "rcUef",
          "name": "History",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "DrLYe",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "History",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "i5s6h",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "See the Log frame below this band.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
