    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "s6IUse",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2461,
      "name": "Log",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "fill": "$surface-container-low",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 12,
      "padding": 28,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "j9t2ZO",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$primary-container",
          "content": "LOG",
          "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "d2lYIx",
          "name": "2026-09-20",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Flow created from the blank starter. Vendored kit 0.1.1 (37 variables: the kit's 34, kit-version-source, plus shell-surface-UNTOKENISED and nav-active-UNTOKENISED held flow-local because the kit has no name for them — see D19). Mirrored Admin / Overview / Default against src/admin/views/pages/overview.html at 6cfefe0, after the period selector was removed and both charts moved onto one time axis. Two token values were found invalid while vendoring: status-ok-fill and overlay-scrim were stored as rgba(), which the .pen schema does not accept. Fixed in both files; the kit bumped to 0.1.1.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "I38f1",
          "name": "2026-09-20b",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Added Admin / Request Logs / Default with its third row expanded. Sidebar copied from Overview and re-pointed rather than rebuilt. Two overflows found and fixed by reading bounds, not by looking: the filter row's fixed select widths left the action group no room, and a sparkline bar was taller than the box that clips it. One more untokenised colour surfaced — #3b1a1a, the Clear All background — now flow-local under D19. Mirrored after the Logs panels stopped claiming 'Last 60m' and 'Today' for a figure that covers the whole retained window.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "iuYJg",
          "name": "2026-09-20c",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Sidebar rebuilt after Adrian caught two defects in it. It had an invented text wordmark where the code loads logo-dark.svg; that file is pure SVG text, so it is now mirrored exactly — '>_ ' in mono, 'She' and 'M' in white, 'LL' in primary-container. Nav labels were sentence case at 13px and are uppercase at 11px with 1.65 tracking, matching font-headline uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-[0.6875rem]. Every item now carries the 4px left border the code gives all of them (transparent when inactive), so labels no longer shift between states. The bottom row (UP uptime + docs, sign-out and GitHub links) and the page footer were missing entirely; 'last read' had been put in the sidebar, where it does not live — it belongs to the degraded banner in main, which is conditional and not drawn. Second defect: Request Logs showed two active nav items, because Update({fill: undefined}) does not clear a fill, it ignores the key. Both sidebars are now built by one function that sets every item explicitly, active or not, and a read-back asserts exactly one is active per screen.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VWK6z",
          "name": "Findings note",
          "fill": "$outline",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "D19 grew by two while mirroring the sidebar: #3b1a1a (Clear All background) and #ffffff (the logo, and text-white throughout the markup). Pure white is not on the palette — on-surface is #e0e3e7.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "GEslu",
          "name": "2026-09-20d",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Added API Keys / Default (third key in edit), Playground / Answered and System / Default. Band complete at 5 of 5. The sidebar is built by one function per screen rather than copied and patched, and every screen is now read back to assert exactly one nav item is active — the check that would have caught the two-highlight bug before Adrian did. One overflow found and fixed by reading bounds on API Keys: the fixed column widths left the Actions cell 68px for three buttons.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "DNDoU",
          "name": "2026-09-20e",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Re-mirrored after the audit close-out landed in code. Overview's queue panel gained the age of the oldest in-flight request and the quota window gained a burn verdict read against the week; System's circuit lines gained a verdict that says what the state costs and what ends it. Two things were drawn and then removed rather than kept: an empty auth verdict, which a healthy provider does not render, and Playground's waiting row, which would have claimed the answer arrived while the page was still waiting. Both are now in states-not-drawn with the reason.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "XboKn",
          "name": "2026-09-20f",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Re-vendored at kit 0.2.0. The four UNTOKENISED locals are gone: D19 gave three of them names in the code (surface-shell, nav-selected, danger-surface) and the fourth is Tailwind's own white, which the markup uses 38 times. 58 nodes repointed, then read back — zero references to a local and zero dangling token references. The suffix did its job: it made the next re-vendor surface them instead of letting them pass as if the kit had always had them.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "j4AA6R",
          "name": "2026-09-20g",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Re-mirrored against dac0bc6 after ten commits moved the views, and drew Sign in / Default — the band is 6 of 6. The code led on that screen and on the CRT treatment, which inverts the source-of-truth rule deliberately (D30, PEN-TODO). Applied in the flow: card titles and section eyebrows are now two levels, 19 nodes moved to on-surface-variant without tracking; Errors sits below Now, because the drawn state has no 5xx and order-1 is Now; the Errors table reports Model, not Route; the second quota window reads Last 18h with the burn rate divided by the hours that actually happened (B5) and the verdict it now renders; the Overview meta row carries '· read'; the Logs summary band moved above the table and onto surface-container without the brand rail. grid-fold-y = 900 is declared and marked on Overview only — the other five screens are shorter than the fold. Not fixed here: the sweep needs a transparent gradient stop the kit has no token for, so #03e3ff00 is the one hex in this flow.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
